/// Which investment-amount validation channel currently fails. Separate channels are never
/// interchangeable: legacy renders a distinct message template per variant, so collapsing two
/// variants into one (or splitting one into two) is a parity defect.
/// 
/// Mirrors `SmartArbitrageManualFragment.checkAmtIsValid`, which has exactly these branches.
/// Exceeding the available balance is deliberately absent: legacy shows a separate, non-blocking
/// `exceedMaxTip` view for that and still permits submit — see `is_over_available_balance`.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]
pub enum SmartArbitrageInvestmentValidity {
    Pristine,
    Valid,
    /// Amount is exactly zero. Legacy uses its own template with a literal `0` minimum, distinct
    /// from `BelowMinimum`'s template, and rejects zero even when no minimum is known.
    Zero,
    BelowMinimum,
    AboveMaximum,
}

