/// Role-keyed convertor set for the Smart Arbitrage detail surface, the sibling of
/// `ContractDcaConvertors`.
/// 
/// Exists because several native sites need a whole CONVERTOR, not just a precision:
/// they render with a rounding mode and a trailing-zero policy
/// (`fundingFeeConvertor.convert(..).keepZero`), which the six-value
/// [`SmartArbDisplayConfig`] cannot express. Native renders these through
/// `BotDisplayTextFormatHelper.text(for:convertor:)` on iOS and
/// `BotDisplayTextRenderer.renderConvertor` on Android.
/// 
/// Precisions and symbols come from the same resolution as the display config, so the
/// two can never disagree.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]
pub struct SmartArbitrageConvertors {
    /// Quote-currency prices. Native `chargeConvertor`.
    pub price: BotConvertor,
    /// Base-coin amounts / stake sizes. Native `tradeConvertor`.
    /// 
    /// Callers must pass an ALREADY-CONVERTED value: native's
    /// `tradeConvertor.toTargetFormatted(x)` performs a unit conversion, which is
    /// arithmetic and therefore Rust's (convertor-surface RFC section 3.4). This role
    /// carries the presentation half only.
    pub amount: BotConvertor,
    /// Funding fee. Keeps trailing zeros: legacy is
    /// `fundingFeeConvertor.convert(..).keepZero`, which pads a bare `0` out to the
    /// funding-fee precision rather than rendering it as `"0"`.
    pub funding_fee: BotConvertor,
    /// Quote-currency amounts (investment, PnL totals).
    pub quote: BotConvertor,
}

